{% set f = r.failed_share %}
{% set rv = r.reversals %}
{% set lvl = (r.settings.level * 100) | int %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Action audit · {{ r.program.name or "AI agent" }}</title>
<style>
{% include "_style.css.j2" %}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Action audit · tickets the AI closed</div>
    <h1>{{ r.program.name or "AI agent" }}</h1>
    <div class="meta">Closures {{ r.period.from }} to {{ r.period.to }} · {{ r.counts.ai_closures | num(0) }} closed by the AI · {{ r.counts.people_closures | num(0) }} by your agents · AI identified by {{ r.counts.flag }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="grade word c-{{ r.confidence.level }}" title="Audit confidence"><div><b>{{ r.confidence.level | capitalize }}</b><small>Audit confidence</small></div></div>
</header>

<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">AI closures that did not stick</div><div class="v">{{ f.estimate | pct }}</div><div class="s">beyond the normal rate · {{ lvl }}% range {{ f.ci_low | pct }} to {{ f.ci_high | pct }}</div></div>
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Reversed after the AI closed them</div><div class="v">{{ rv.ai_rate | pct(1) }}</div><div class="s">{{ rv.ai_reopened | pct(1) }} reopened · {{ rv.ai_repeat | pct(1) }} repeat ticket</div></div>
  <div class="tile"><div class="k">Reversed after your agents closed them</div><div class="v">{{ rv.people_rate | pct(1) }}</div><div class="s">same issue types and months</div></div>
</div>

<p class="headline">{{ r.headline }}</p>

<h2><span class="num">1</span>What was checked</h2>
<p>An action that has to be undone is not saved work. A ticket the AI closed counts as reversed if it was reopened, or if the same person opened a ticket {% if r.settings.match == "same_type" %}about the same type of issue {% endif %}within {{ r.settings.window_days }} days. The same check runs on tickets your agents closed, weighted to the same issue mix and months, and only the excess counts against the AI.</p>
<p class="callout info">Did not stick = (reversed after the AI − reversed after people) ÷ (1 − reversed after people)</p>

{% if r.by_type %}
<h2><span class="num">2</span>By type of issue</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Type</th><th class="n">AI closures</th><th class="n">Reversed (AI)</th><th class="n">Reversed (people)</th><th class="n">Did not stick</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for t in r.by_type %}<tr><td>{{ t.work_type }}</td><td class="n">{{ t.claims | num(0) }}</td><td class="n">{{ t.ai_return_rate | pct(1) }}</td><td class="n">{{ t.baseline_return_rate | pct(1) }}</td><td class="n">{{ t.failed_share | pct }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}

{% if r.by_month %}
<h2><span class="num">3</span>By month</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Month</th><th class="n">AI closures</th><th class="n">Reversed (AI)</th><th class="n">Reversed (people)</th><th class="n">Did not stick</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for m in r.by_month %}<tr><td>{{ m.month }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.closures | num(0) }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.ai_rate | pct(1) }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.people_rate | pct(1) }}</td><td class="n">{{ m.failed_share | pct }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}

<h2><span class="num">4</span>Audit confidence: {{ r.confidence.level }}</h2>
<ul>{% for reason in r.confidence.reasons %}<li>{{ reason }}</li>{% endfor %}{% for n in r.notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<p class="meta">Probative Labs {{ r.lineage.code.probative }} · settings <span class="mono">{{ r.lineage.settings_sha256[:12] }}</span> · {{ r.lineage.interval }} · run {{ r.lineage.run_at }}</p>
<footer>Generated by Probative Labs, independent verification of what AI delivers. Evaluates the AI's actions, never people. Method: docs/action-audit.md.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
